{"type": "tool_call", "n": 62, "ts": 1790151556.5546272, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "US ENTITY \u2014 MARCH 2026 OPERATING EXPENSE FLUX vs FEBRUARY 2026 (USD)\nPrepared by: david.murguia@gmail.com | Date: 2026-04-03 | Checklist item \"Flux review\" set to in_progress\n\n=====================================================================\n1. SUMMARY\n=====================================================================\nTotal US operating expense:  Feb 2026 $261,750.70  \u2192  Mar 2026 $295,463.10\nChange: +$33,712.40 (+12.9%)\n\nThree lines breach the threshold (>10% AND >$5,000). All three are increases:\n\nAcct  Line                      Feb          Mar          $ Var        % Var\n5000  Hosting & Infrastructure   31,301.80    40,948.20    +9,646.40    +30.8%\n6300  Travel                        785.40     7,158.41    +6,373.01   +811.4%\n6400  Marketing Programs          7,898.14    29,686.00   +21,787.86   +275.9%\n                                                          -----------\n                                   Threshold breaches:     +37,807.27\n                                   All other lines, net:    -4,094.87\n                                   Total variance:         +33,712.40\n\nNo expense line declined by more than 10% and $5,000.\n\n=====================================================================\n2. EXPLANATIONS \u2014 LINES OVER THRESHOLD\n=====================================================================\n\n--- 5000 HOSTING & INFRASTRUCTURE: +$9,646.40 (+30.8%) \u2014 SUPPORTED ---\nDriver is a single non-recurring item; the recurring run-rate was actually flat-to-down.\n  \u2022 JE-00258 (3/14) Stackline Cloud inv. SC-M-2203 \u2014 one-time data migration: $9,800.00.\n    Non-recurring; should not repeat in April.\n  \u2022 JE-00232 (3/03) Stackline Cloud inv. STA-98877 \u2014 cloud infrastructure, production:\n    $31,148.20, vs. Feb's JE-00125 (2/03) inv. STA-12523 of $31,301.80. Recurring\n    hosting DECREASED $153.60 (-0.5%).\n  Bridge: +9,800.00 (one-time migration) - 153.60 (recurring) = +9,646.40. Fully explained.\n  Both March entries carry vendor invoice support. Driver holds up.\n\n--- 6400 MARKETING PROGRAMS: +$21,787.86 (+275.9%) \u2014 SUPPORTED ---\nTwo new March vendor invoices account for 100.0% of the March balance:\n  \u2022 JE-00241 (3/06) Meridian Events inv. ME-0588 \u2014 SaaS Connect Spring conference\n    sponsorship, event dates 3/17\u20133/19: $22,000.00. Event-driven, non-recurring.\n  \u2022 JE-00243 (3/06) Oakridge Creative inv. OAK-10546 \u2014 content and campaign services:\n    $7,686.00.\n  $22,000.00 + $7,686.00 = $29,686.00 = March 6400 activity exactly. Both invoice-supported.\n  Note on period fit: the sponsored event ran 3/17\u20133/19, i.e. the benefit was delivered\n  inside March, so full expensing in March is appropriate \u2014 no deferral required. Driver holds up.\n\n--- 6300 TRAVEL: +$6,373.01 (+811.4%) \u2014 *** DRIVER DOES NOT HOLD UP *** ---\nRoutine card-based travel was essentially flat month over month:\n  Feb card activity $785.40 (JE-00132 Uber 31.36; JE-00167 Delta 420.62; JE-00188 Uber 38.32;\n  JE-00196 Hilton 295.10)\n  Mar card activity $858.41 (JE-00266 Hilton 197.45; JE-00269 Delta 566.47; JE-00277 Uber 53.29;\n  JE-00298 Uber 41.20) \u2014 only +$73.01 (+9.3%), which on its own would NOT breach the threshold.\n\n  The entire variance is one entry:\n  \u2022 JE-00300 (3/29) \"Travel reimbursement - T. Vance\", $6,300.00, Dr 6300 / Cr 1000\n    Cash - Operating. Source = MANUAL. has_support = FALSE.\n\n  Why I am not accepting this as an explanation:\n    (a) No supporting documentation is attached \u2014 no expense report, no receipts, no approval.\n        I could not locate substantiation, so I am not able to attach support to it.\n    (b) It is a manual journal, not a card feed or AP item, and it credits operating cash\n        directly rather than clearing through Employee Advances (1450) or AP (2000) \u2014 so\n        there is no reimbursement request to tie it to.\n    (c) The amount is suspiciously round ($6,300.00) and is dated 3/29, two days before\n        period end, in a month where all other travel totaled $858. It is 88.0% of the\n        March travel line.\n    (d) It should also be confirmed to have cleared the bank; if it has not, the cash credit\n        is unsupported as well.\n\n  RECOMMENDATION: Do not report the Travel flux as \"explained.\" Obtain T. Vance's expense\n  report and receipts. If substantiation cannot be produced, reverse JE-00300 (or reclass to\n  1450 Employee Advances pending documentation). Excluding JE-00300, Travel is +$73.01 (+9.3%)\n  and is a non-reportable variance. Please treat this as an open exception for controller review.\n  (I intended to log this via flag_exception but exhausted the tool-call budget before doing so \u2014\n  it is raised here instead and needs to be recorded.)\n\n=====================================================================\n3. LINES BELOW THRESHOLD \u2014 NOTED BUT NOT REPORTABLE\n=====================================================================\n  6000 Salaries & Wages     183,800.38 \u2192 184,465.91   +665.53  (+0.4%)  normal\n  6010 Payroll Taxes         14,060.73 \u2192  14,111.64    +50.91  (+0.4%)  tracks salaries\n  6100 Rent                  14,500.00 \u2192  14,500.00      0.00           fixed lease\n  6110 Utilities                919.82 \u2192     922.22     +2.40  (+0.3%)\n  6200 Software Subs          4,139.80 \u2192   3,339.50   -800.30  (-19.3%) % but not $\n  6310 Meals & Ent.             114.32 \u2192      49.75    -64.57  (-56.5%) immaterial\n  6320 Training & Conf.         542.56 \u2192       0.00   -542.56  (-100%)  immaterial\n  6600 Office Supplies          197.75 \u2192     281.47    +83.72  (+42.3%) immaterial\n  6900 Bank Fees                 65.00 \u2192       0.00    -65.00  (-100%)  see below\n  6800 Depreciation           3,425.00 \u2192       0.00 -3,425.00  (-100%)  see below\n  Nil in both months: 5100, 5200, 6020, 6030, 6120, 6410, 6500, 6510, 6520, 6550, 6700, 6950, 7100\n\n=====================================================================\n4. IMPORTANT CAVEAT \u2014 THE FLUX IS PRELIMINARY\n=====================================================================\nMarch close is not finished, and several US checklist items that hit operating expense are\nstill OPEN. March opex is therefore UNDERSTATED and the variances above will move:\n\n  \u2022 \"Record depreciation\" \u2014 OPEN. Account 6800 has $0.00 of March activity vs. $3,425.00 in\n    February. This is not a real -100% decline; the entry simply has not been booked. Expect\n    ~$3,425 to be added to March, which will reduce the reported total opex increase.\n  \u2022 \"Amortize prepaid software\" \u2014 OPEN. Likely additional charge to 6200 (Software\n    Subscriptions currently shows a $800.30 decline, which may reverse once amortization posts).\n  \u2022 \"Accrue unpaid payroll\" \u2014 OPEN. Salaries (6000) and Payroll Taxes (6010) are currently\n    almost exactly flat vs. February (+0.4%), which is itself a flag that the March accrual\n    has not yet been recorded. If a material accrual posts, 6000 could become a\n    threshold-breaching line and would need its own explanation.\n  \u2022 \"AP cutoff review\" \u2014 OPEN. Unrecorded March vendor invoices could add to 5000/6400/others.\n\n  Also note 6900 Bank Fees at $0.00 for March vs. $65.00 in February \u2014 small, but consistent\n  with bank reconciliations still being open; the March service charge may simply not be\n  booked yet.\n\nI did not post any journal entries as part of this analysis. No entry was posted for\nJE-00300 because I could not obtain support, per policy.\n\n=====================================================================\n5. ACTIONS REQUESTED FROM CONTROLLER\n=====================================================================\n  1. Obtain or reject support for JE-00300 ($6,300, T. Vance travel reimbursement). Until then,\n     the Travel flux is unexplained and should not be signed off. Recommend reversal or\n     reclass to 1450 if documentation is not produced.\n  2. Re-run this flux after depreciation, prepaid software amortization, payroll accrual and\n     AP cutoff are posted. Salaries and Software Subscriptions in particular should be\n     re-tested against the 10%/$5,000 threshold at that point.\n  3. Confirm the $9,800 Stackline data migration (JE-00258) and the $22,000 Meridian\n     sponsorship (JE-00241) are flagged as non-recurring for April forecasting \u2014 together they\n     are $31,800 of the $33,712 total increase.\n"}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 7}
